{
 "_comment": "Which janko.at puzzles this fork ships, and why the list exists. The generator's gate (unique / line-solvable / fills-its-grid) is a property of the CLUES and cannot see the finished picture at all: a puzzle can pass all three and solve into a scatter of blobs nobody can name. So the keep/drop call is a judgement made by looking, and this file is that judgement, committed so the bank is reproducible. Feed it to import_picross.py --ids. The drop list is recorded too, so a second opinion can disagree with a specific puzzle rather than with a rate. Only the first pass's drops are absent: it recorded keeps alone, and its 109 drops are the judged ids missing from both lists.",
 "method": "One agent looked at every picture in these batches at ~90px and asked one question: could I name the subject WITHOUT the caption? Recognisable object or scene = keep. Abstract pattern, dense noise, or a shape I could only name after being told = drop. This is a judgement, not a filter: the gate (unique / line-solvable / fills-its-grid) is a property of the CLUES and cannot see the picture at all. SECOND PASS (the remaining 251): identical question and identical thumbnail scale, but read from contact sheets of 48 rather than a few at a time, calling out the drops. Same evidence the player gets -- 9px cells at 10x10 and 6px at 15x15 is the ~90px picture the PICKER draws a solved tile at, so a picture that only reads when blown up is a false keep and is dropped here.",
